---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import siteData from '../content/siteData.json';

const now = new Date();
const start = new Date(now.getFullYear(), 0, 0);
const diff = now.getTime() - start.getTime();
const dayOfYear = Math.floor(diff / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));

const themeIndex = dayOfYear % siteData.themes.length;
const colorIndex = dayOfYear % siteData.colorSchemes.length;
const todayTheme = siteData.themes[themeIndex];
const todayColor = siteData.colorSchemes[colorIndex];
const todayFact = todayTheme.facts[dayOfYear % todayTheme.facts.length];
const todayQuote = todayTheme.quotes[dayOfYear % todayTheme.quotes.length];
const changelogEntries = siteData.changelog.entries.slice(-5).reverse();

const colorData = JSON.stringify({
  primary: todayColor.primary,
  secondary: todayColor.secondary,
  accent: todayColor.accent,
  background: todayColor.background,
  text: todayColor.text,
  shader: todayColor.shaderParams
});
---

<BaseLayout>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
       HERO
  ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="hero" class="hero">
    <div id="moonContainer">
      <div id="moonShadow"></div>
      <pre id="asciiMoon"></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="logo-sanskrit">अत्रिज</div>
    <div class="logo-subtitle">Atrij</div>
    <p class="logo-tagline">An <em>impressionist</em> journey through light, philosophy &amp; the cosmos</p>
    <span class="scroll-hint">Scroll to explore</span>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
       TODAY'S REFLECTION
  ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="today" class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">Today's Reflection</div>
      <h2>What the <em>universe</em> whispers today</h2>
      <div class="today-fact">
        <div class="theme-tag">{todayTheme.title} · {todayColor.mood}</div>
        <p>{todayFact.text}</p>
        <div class="source">{todayFact.source}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="quote-block">
        <p>{todayQuote}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
       I. THE MOON — SELENE
  ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="moon" class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">I. The Moon</div>
      <h2>Selene's <em>silver</em> chariot</h2>
      <p>In the beginning, there was darkness — and then Selene rose. The ancient Greeks saw her as a silver chariot crossing the night sky, but she was more than a goddess. She was the first mirror, the original reflector of light, the celestial body that taught humanity that one can shine without being the source.</p>

      <div class="image-card" style="--card-bg-image: url('/images/moon.svg')">
        <div class="card-bg"></div>
        <div class="card-content">
          <p>{siteData.themes[0].facts[0].text}</p>
          <div class="source">{siteData.themes[0].facts[0].source}</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="facts-group">
        {siteData.themes[0].facts.slice(1, 3).map((fact, i) => (
          <div class="fact-card">
            <div class="fact-number">Fact {i + 1}</div>
            <p>{fact.text}</p>
            <div class="source">{fact.source}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="quote-block">
        <p>{siteData.themes[0].quotes[0]}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
       II. THE WAVES — EGO & ARROGANCE
  ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="philosophy" class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">II. The Waves</div>
      <h2>Ego, arrogance &amp; the <em>ocean</em> of self</h2>
      <p>The wave does not know it is the ocean. It rises, believes itself unique, crashes against the shore, and dissolves — only to rise again. This is the cycle of ego: the endless assertion of separateness against the vast indifference of the sea.</p>

      <div class="image-card" style="--card-bg-image: url('/images/waves.svg')">
        <div class="card-bg"></div>
        <div class="card-content">
          <p>{siteData.themes[1].facts[0].text}</p>
          <div class="source">{siteData.themes[1].facts[0].source}</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="facts-group">
        {siteData.themes[1].facts.slice(1, 3).map((fact, i) => (
          <div class="fact-card">
            <div class="fact-number">Fact {i + 1}</div>
            <p>{fact.text}</p>
            <div class="source">{fact.source}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="quote-block">
        <p>{siteData.themes[1].quotes[0]}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
       III. THE BATTLEFIELD — BHAGAVAD GITA
  ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="gita" class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">III. The Battlefield</div>
      <h2>Wisdom from the <em>Bhagavad</em> Gita</h2>
      <p>On the battlefield of Kurukshetra, between two armies of cousins, a conversation took place that would echo through millennia. Arjuna, paralyzed by doubt, and Krishna, the charioteer who was also God — their dialogue is not about war. It is about the war within.</p>

      <div class="image-card" style="--card-bg-image: url('/images/stars.svg')">
        <div class="card-bg"></div>
        <div class="card-content">
          <p>{siteData.themes[2].facts[0].text}</p>
          <div class="source">{siteData.themes[2].facts[0].source}</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="facts-group">
        {siteData.themes[2].facts.slice(1, 4).map((fact, i) => (
          <div class="fact-card">
            <div class="fact-number">Fact {i + 1}</div>
            <p>{fact.text}</p>
            <div class="source">{fact.source}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="quote-block">
        <p>{siteData.themes[2].quotes[1]}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
       IV. THE DANCE — SHIV PURANA
  ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="shiva" class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">IV. The Dance</div>
      <h2>Shiva &amp; the <em>cosmic</em> rhythm</h2>
      <p>Before there was creation, there was Shiva — not as a being, but as a possibility. The Shiv Purana does not begin with "In the beginning" but with "In the endless." Shiva is the stillness that contains all motion, the silence that holds all music.</p>

      <div class="image-card" style="--card-bg-image: url('/images/flute.svg')">
        <div class="card-bg"></div>
        <div class="card-content">
          <p>{siteData.themes[3].facts[0].text}</p>
          <div class="source">{siteData.themes[3].facts[0].source}</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="facts-group">
        {siteData.themes[3].facts.slice(1, 4).map((fact, i) => (
          <div class="fact-card">
            <div class="fact-number">Fact {i + 1}</div>
            <p>{fact.text}</p>
            <div class="source">{fact.source}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="quote-block">
        <p>{siteData.themes[3].quotes[0]}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
       V. THE CANVAS — ART & BEAUTY
  ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="art" class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">V. The Canvas</div>
      <h2>Art, beauty &amp; the <em>act</em> of seeing</h2>
      <p>Art is not what you see, but what you make others see. The painter does not copy the world — they translate it, filtering reality through the lens of emotion, memory, and dream. Every brushstroke is a meditation, every color a prayer.</p>

      <div class="image-card" style="--card-bg-image: url('/images/sunflowers.svg')">
        <div class="card-bg"></div>
        <div class="card-content">
          <p>{siteData.themes[4].facts[0].text}</p>
          <div class="source">{siteData.themes[4].facts[0].source}</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="facts-group">
        {siteData.themes[4].facts.slice(1, 3).map((fact, i) => (
          <div class="fact-card">
            <div class="fact-number">Fact {i + 1}</div>
            <p>{fact.text}</p>
            <div class="source">{fact.source}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="quote-block">
        <p>{siteData.themes[4].quotes[0]}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
       CHANGELOG
  ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="changelog" class="section">
    <div class="section-inner changelog-section">
      <div class="section-label">Changelog</div>
      <h2>Daily <em>mutations</em></h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: var(--text-sm); margin-bottom: var(--space-xl); font-family: var(--font-sans);">
        Version {siteData.changelog.version} — color, content &amp; form evolve daily.
      </p>
      <div class="changelog-timeline">
        {changelogEntries.map(entry => (
          <div class="changelog-entry">
            <div class="changelog-entry-header">
              <span class="changelog-date">{entry.date}</span>
              <span class={'changelog-type type-' + entry.type}>
                {entry.type === 'initial' && '✦'}
                {entry.type === 'feature' && '◆'}
                {entry.type === 'fix' && '◈'}
                {entry.type === 'content' && '✎'}
                {entry.type === 'design' && '◐'}
                {' '}{entry.type}
              </span>
              <span class="changelog-version">v{siteData.changelog.version}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="changelog-desc">{entry.description}</div>
            <ul class="changelog-changes">
              {entry.changes.map(change => (
                <li>{change}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
       THREE.JS SCENE INIT
  ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div id="vg-data" data-colors={colorData} hidden></div>
  <script>
    (function() {
      var el = document.getElementById('vg-data');
      var c = JSON.parse(el.dataset.colors);
      var r = document.documentElement.style;
      r.setProperty('--color-primary', c.primary);
      r.setProperty('--color-secondary', c.secondary);
      r.setProperty('--color-accent', c.accent);
      r.setProperty('--color-bg', c.background);
      r.setProperty('--color-text', c.text);
      window.__VG_SHADER = c.shader;
    })();
  </script>
  <script type="module" src="/js/scene-init.js"></script>

  <!-- ── ASCII Moon: Galileo spacecraft photo art + shadow phase animation ── -->
  <style>
    #moonContainer {
      position: relative;
      border-radius: 50%;
      overflow: hidden;
      width: clamp(180px, 35vw, 340px);
      height: clamp(180px, 35vw, 340px);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
      box-shadow: 0 0 60px 10px rgba(255,213,79,0.08), 0 0 120px 30px rgba(255,213,79,0.04);
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    #moonShadow {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0; left: 0;
      width: 100%; height: 100%;
      background-color: rgba(8,8,15,0.85);
      box-shadow: 0 0 2rem rgba(8,8,15,0.9);
      border-radius: 50%;
      transform: translateX(0%);
      transition: transform 1.2s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
      pointer-events: none;
      z-index: 2;
    }
    #asciiMoon {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
      text-align: center;
      font-size: clamp(2.2px, 0.42vw, 4.5px);
      line-height: 1.35;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      box-sizing: border-box;
      background-color: #08080f;
      color: #c9a84c;
      text-shadow: 0 0 1px rgba(201,168,76,0.3);
      white-space: pre;
      overflow: hidden;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-family: 'Courier New', 'Lucida Console', monospace;
    }
    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      #moonContainer {
        width: clamp(140px, 45vw, 220px);
        height: clamp(140px, 45vw, 220px);
      }
      #asciiMoon {
        font-size: clamp(1.8px, 0.55vw, 3px);
        line-height: 1.4;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
